1
00:00:00,064 --> 00:00:01,894
(Amy:)How long do you think
you can keep it from him?

2
00:00:01,899 --> 00:00:04,729
(Bernadette:)Yeah, isn't it gonna get
worse the longer you wait?

3
00:00:04,735 --> 00:00:06,265
(Penny:)Well, not necessarily.

4
00:00:06,270 --> 00:00:08,100
(Penny:)You know,
Dad's not getting any younger,

5
00:00:08,105 --> 00:00:09,705
(Penny:)so if I wait long enough,

6
00:00:09,707 --> 00:00:11,477
(Penny:)I'll just tell him
he walked me down the aisle

7
00:00:11,475 --> 00:00:13,005
(Penny:)and it was magical.

8
00:00:18,148 --> 00:00:20,318
(Raj:)When did you learn
how to change a tire?

9
00:00:20,317 --> 00:00:22,687
(Howard:)Every self-respecting gentleman
should know how

10
00:00:22,686 --> 00:00:24,986
(Howard:)in case he comes across
a damsel in distress

11
00:00:24,989 --> 00:00:26,489
(Howard:)by the side of the road.

12
00:00:27,824 --> 00:00:28,994
(Sheldon:)If I see one scorpion,

13
00:00:28,993 --> 00:00:30,363
(Sheldon:)I am getting
on someone's shoulders

14
00:00:30,361 --> 00:00:32,391
(Sheldon:)and never coming down.

15
00:00:32,396 --> 00:00:34,626
(Leonard:)And there's your damsel.

16
00:00:35,965 --> 00:00:38,335
(Howard:)Wow, this one's really stuck.

17
00:00:38,335 --> 00:00:39,965
(Raj:)Are you turning
it the right way?

18
00:00:39,970 --> 00:00:41,540
(Sheldon:)No.

19
00:00:41,539 --> 00:00:42,809
(Howard:)I took the other four off

20
00:00:42,807 --> 00:00:44,337
(Howard:)and when I got to this one,
I thought,

21
00:00:44,341 --> 00:00:46,211
"You know, I'm in a rut.
Let's shake things up."

22
00:00:46,210 --> 00:00:48,080
(Raj:)Here, let me try.

23
00:00:49,279 --> 00:00:51,579
(grunting)

24
00:00:54,551 --> 00:01:04,021
(Raj:)You're right, it doesn't turn
the other way.

